X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Libcal Bccls 10306": "https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17784881"}
X-SOURCE-ID:libcal_bccls_10306
X-SOURCE:Libcal Bccls 10306
DTSTART:20261112T181500Z
DTEND:20261112T191500Z
DTSTAMP:20261112T000000Z
SUMMARY:CANCELLED!! Everything Book Club\,  "London Falling:" by Patrick Radden Keefe
DESCRIPTION:SEE SESSION 1 on Tuesday\, Nov. 10. Goes with the Open Book / 
 Open Mind program with Patrick Radden Keefe about "London Falling: A 
 Mysterious Death in a Gilded City and a Family's Search for Truth" the 
 following week on Tuesday\, November 17! Tickets cost $40 and include a 
 signed copy of the book. (If for any reason you can't afford a ticket\, 
 come talk to me.)\n\nWe'll talk about Keefe's conversation as well as 
 "London Falling\," a literary true crime investigation into the tragic 
 death of a 19-year-old boy who\, as it turns out\, was masquerading as an 
 oligarch's son in London's seamy underworld. \n\n“Gripping. . . . Keefe 
 is a master at using true crime as a vehicle for exploring social and 
 political pathologies.”\n—NPR\n\n\n\n\nGenerally considered one of our 
 greatest living non-fiction writers\, PATRICK RADDEN KEEFE is a staff 
 writer at The New Yorker and the author of The New York Times bestsellers 
 "Rogues\," "Empire of Pain" (winner of the 2021 Baillie Gifford Prize) and 
 "Say Nothing\," which received the National Book Critics Circle Award and 
 was named one of the Twenty Best Books of the 21st Century by The New York 
 Times Book Review. Keefe served as an Executive Producer on the 
 award-winning FX series “Say Nothing\,” based on his book. \n\n\n\n\n
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Tower Room\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult Services, Book Discussion
UID:LibCal-10306-17784881
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17784881
END:VEVENT
