SUMMARY:Parent Workshop: Learning to Read\, Let's talk about Decoding (adults only)
DESCRIPTION:The Library’s Reading Specialist will be hosting her first 
 parent workshop of the 2026-2027 school year. This will be the first of 3 
 workshops in a series about Literacy. Parents\, caregivers and reading 
 tutors will learn about the Science of Reading and the process of learning 
 how to read. We will also discuss how to support your child’s literacy 
 learning at home. Lastly\, participants will learn about the resources 
 available to check out of the library and how to use them at home. 
 Registration required.\n\nThis is a hybrid event. You will receive the link 
 after registering.\n\n(The 2nd workshop about Reading Comprehension will 
 take place in December. The 3rd workshop of the series about Writing will 
 take place in January.)\n\n \n\n
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Storytime Room
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Children's Programs, Reading Specialist
UID:LibCal-10306-17802350
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17802350
END:VEVENT
