X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Libcal Bccls 10341": "https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17488200"}
X-SOURCE-ID:libcal_bccls_10341
X-SOURCE:Libcal Bccls 10341
DTSTART:20261114T190000Z
DTEND:20261114T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20261114T000000Z
SUMMARY:John Lennon: Life\, Legend\, and Legacy
DESCRIPTION:A presentation by John Paul Groom\n\nAbout the program \n\nThe 
 beginning of The Beatles took place at a summer garden fete at St. Peter's 
 Church in Woolton\, Liverpool\, on July 6\, 1957\, marking a watershed 
 point in music history. When John Lennon was 16 years old and performing 
 with his skiffle band The Quarrymen\, a common acquaintance called Ivan 
 Vaughan\, introduced him to Paul McCartney\, who was 15 years old at the 
 time. This one-of-a-kind partnership altered the course of music 
 irrevocably\, and our presenter will trace its history.\n\nAbout the 
 presenter\n\nJohn Paul Groom gives historical presentations about the 
 1960s\, with a particular focus on The Beatles. Originally from Liverpool\, 
 Groom resided in the same city as John Lennon and George Harrison\, 
 participated in the same Sunday school as John Lennon\, and went to the 
 same high school as Paul McCartney and George Harrison.  \n\n
LOCATION:West Orange - Community Room 1
ORGANIZER;CN="West Orange Library":MAILTO:events@westorange.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:Lecture
UID:LibCal-10341-17488200
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17488200
END:VEVENT
