DTSTART:20261121T190000Z
DTEND:20261121T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20261121T000000Z
SUMMARY:Winter Seed Sowing Workshop
DESCRIPTION:You don't have to wait until Spring to plan your garden -- in 
 fact\, Winter is the best time to start native seeds.\n\nNative plants are 
 a beautiful\, beneficial addition to any garden. And growing plants from 
 seed is an easy\, low cost way to add native plants to your landscaping. In 
 this free workshop\, using seeds from the Glen Ridge Native Seed Library\, 
 learn how to prepare your native seeds so they are ready to grow next 
 Spring. This process is called cold stratification\, which will be 
 explained with a how-to demonstration of the various methods you can use. 
 Choose from 90 New Jersey native species and get recommendations for your 
 yard based on growing conditions\, color\, and height. Learn how to grow 
 native plants with confidence and best practices for supporting wildlife in 
 your yard.\n\nSponsored by the Glen Ridge Environmental Advisory Committee.
LOCATION:Glen Ridge - Meeting Room\, Glen Ridge Free Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Glen Ridge Library":MAILTO:events@glenridgelibrary.org
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-10286-17822730
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17822730
END:VEVENT
