DTSTAMP:20261107T055436Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261206T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261206T120000
SUMMARY:SMC Trail Work Volunteer Day
DESCRIPTION:South Mountain Conservancy Activities Meetup Group\n**TRAIL WO
 RK will continue rerouting the Hogenauer Trail** (we are almost finished!)
  up the slope and away from recently installed property fences. **Meet At:
 ** Dog Park/ Wildflower Preserve\, 11 Bear Lane\, Maplewood. From there\, 
 we will walk to Crater View on Crest drive and then to the Hogenauer trail
  work site.\n\nTrail work is physically challenging but very satisfying as
  we use hand tools to build and repair trails. Participants must be 15+ ye
 ars. Those younger than 18 must be accompanied by an adult. Participants *
 *should wear long pants** due to [ticks](https://www.somocon.org/?page_id=
 193928&fb) and thron bushes and sturdy shoes\, and bring gloves (though ba
 ckup gloves will be available). Tools\, water\, and a snack will be provid
 ed. (Registration is not required though if you sign up on Meetup\, it hel
 ps us know how many tools to bring.) Only heavy\, steady rain cancels.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/somocon/events/317304154/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261105T202300Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261105T202300Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
