DTEND:20261211T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20261210T000000Z
SUMMARY:Astrology 101: What's Your Sign?
DESCRIPTION:Thursday\, December 10\, 2026 from 6:00 PM to 8:00 PM.\n\nNo 
 registration required! \n\nLet's talk astrology! This program will provide 
 a basic overview of Western astrology\, including the twelve zodiac signs\, 
 the four elements and three modalities\, the ten traditional planets\, and 
 the five major aspects.\n\nThis program is a lecture-style PowerPoint 
 presentation with Q&A woven throughout. The focus here is not on "sun sign 
 astrology" (analyzing personalities based simply on the twelve zodiac 
 signs)\, but rather on gaining a bird's eye view of the larger astrological 
 system\, of which sun signs are just one part. You will leave the program 
 with the information you need to look at an astrology chart and decode its 
 many glyphs — the ancient symbols that represent the key foundational 
 concepts of this archetypal language.\n\nAttendees are strongly encouraged 
 to look up their natal charts in advance on any number of free websites. 
 Although Kate will not have time to provide personalized chart 
 interpretations\, you will be invited to apply key concepts to your own 
 chart as we go. (Hard copy or digital is fine.)  You may also want to bring 
 a notebook and pen. While Astrology 101 is designed with total beginners in 
 mind\, some familiarity with the twelve zodiac signs\, especially your own 
 sign\, is helpful. More intermediate astrology learners may benefit from 
 this jam-packed review of foundational concepts. \n\nMore about natal 
 charts: The phrase "natal chart" involves using not only the day of your 
 birth\, but also the exact place and the exact time of your birth\, in 
 order to look at your Sun\, Moon\, Rising as well as the traditional 
 planets Mercury\, Venus\, Mars\, Jupiter\, and Saturn\, and the modern 
 planets Uranus\, Neptune\, and Pluto. Anyone who does not know and cannot 
 access their exact time of birth can still get a lot out of Astrology 101. 
 They can look up everything apart from the rising/ascendant sign. Below is 
 an example chart generated by the free website astro.com! You can bring a 
 print out or digital copy of your chart to the program!\n\n\n\n \n\nAbout 
 the presenter: Kate Sheridan\, a.k.a. The Laundress\, is a tarot reader and 
 astrologer who believes that each one of us can make our own magic. Her 
 approach is healing rather than predictive\, and her work is deeply 
 informed by Jungian psychology. You can find her on Instagram 
 @themodernlaundress or online at thelaundresstarot.com.
LOCATION:Nutley - Stockton Room\, Nutley Free Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Nutley Library":MAILTO:events@nutley.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-10315-17779987
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17779987
END:VEVENT
