X-SOURCE-ID:libcal_bccls_10341
X-SOURCE:Libcal Bccls 10341
DTSTART:20261218T160000Z
DTEND:20261218T170000Z
DTSTAMP:20261218T000000Z
SUMMARY:December Book Club: Beautyland
DESCRIPTION:A book club for adults who want to read in community. We meet 
 one Friday morning a month to chat about a title we read in 
 common.\n\n--\n\nBEAUTYLAND\nby Marie-Helene Bertino (2024)\n\nA wise\, 
 tender novel about a woman who doesn't feel at home on Earth: At the moment 
 when Voyager 1 is launched into space\, a baby of unusual perception is 
 born to a single mother in Philadelphia. Adina Giorno is tiny and 
 jaundiced\, but reaches for warmth and light. As a child\, she recognizes 
 that she is different\; she also possesses knowledge of a faraway planet 
 and is here to report on the oddities of earthlings. For years\, as she 
 moves through the world and makes a life for herself among humans\, she 
 dispatches transmissions on the terrors and surprising joys of their 
 existence. --publisher\n\nCopies will be available at the Circulation Desk 
 starting November 20. \n\n
LOCATION:Literacy Room\, West Orange Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="West Orange Library":MAILTO:events@westorange.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:Book Club
UID:LibCal-10341-17302637
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17302637
END:VEVENT
